    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Plugmint – Sticky Notes for Posts, Pages, Products &amp; CPTs plugin lets adminis to attach short  notes inside the post editor. Notes are stored as post meta and are not visible on the front-end.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the <code>plugmint-sticky-notes</code> folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Go to Settings <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Post Page Notes to exclude any post types where you don&#8217;t want notes.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='are%20notes%20visible%20on%20the%20front-end%3F'>\nAre notes visible on the front-end?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. Notes are stored as post meta and are only shown inside the WordPress admin.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='can%20i%20exclude%20custom%20post%20types%3F'>\nCan I exclude custom post types?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Use Settings <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Post Page Notes to choose which public post types to exclude.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='can%20you%20create%20a%20plugin%20for%20me%3F'>\nCan you create a plugin for me?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes! i&#8217;m offering a custom plugin development service. Contact me at ridwansweb@gmail.com.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "A lightweight plugin to add private admin-only notes to posts, pages, products and on any custom post types.",
    "description": "<p>Plugmint – Sticky Notes for Posts, Pages, Products &amp; CPTs plugin lets adminis to attach short  notes inside the post editor. Notes are stored as post meta and are not visible on the front-end.</p>\n",
